<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 517 mln stg further help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 517 mln stg further help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with a further 517 million stg of assistance at established interest rates.</p>
<p>It allotted 342 million stg outright in bills and 175 million stg in repos to September 1.</p>
<p>The Bank has now provided liquidity totalling 1.637 billion stg so far on Friday, in response to a revised money market shortage forecast of 1.95 billion stg.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7708</p>
